# Root-level JSON allowlist: block every *.json file directly in the repo
# root except the two known-legitimate config files. This is the primary
# guard against ad hoc test/debug JSON (curl output, manual proof capture,
# etc.) landing at repo root and silently accumulating again - name-pattern
# rules alone only catch filenames that happen to match a known prefix.
# Does not affect subdirectories (apps/web/*.json, drizzle/migrations/**,
# services/api/*.json, etc.) since the leading "/" anchors to root only.
/*.json
!/package.json
!/tsconfig.json

# Scratch test/debug output written by the AI assistant - belt-and-suspenders
# for the same class of file outside repo root, or if the allowlist above is
# ever loosened - never commit.
dedup*.json
search*.json
payload*.json
*-result.json
*-debug.json
*.debug.json
test-output*

# Generated CV/cover letter output files - not source
services/api/storage/

# Browser automation screenshots - never commit
tmp-browser-proof/
